# PART 16 — PRODUCT APPROVAL WORKFLOW

A product submitted by a seller must pass through the review workflow.

Suggested lifecycle:

Draft → Submitted → Under Review → Approved → Published.

Other possible outcomes:

- Changes Required.
- Rejected.
- Suspended.
- Archived.

The Founder can review everything.

An assigned Product Team member may review, request changes, approve or publish products only when the Founder has explicitly assigned the relevant capability.

A product cannot bypass the review process.

When changes are required, the seller should receive a useful explanation through the existing notification system.

When approved, the listing can become publicly visible according to its publication status and stock availability.

The approval process must never be controlled by a seller.

Record reviewer identity and decision history.

