## Critical security requirements

1. Implement or preserve RLS.
2. Sellers can read and modify only their own authorized seller data.
3. Employees can access only functions granted to them.
4. Only the Founder has unrestricted platform administration privileges.
5. Sellers cannot approve their own products.
6. Sellers cannot modify verification status.
7. Employees cannot modify their own permissions.
8. Employees cannot grant Founder privileges.
9. Sellers cannot access other sellers' orders or private documents.
10. Sensitive verification documents must not be publicly accessible.
11. All important privileged actions must be checked server-side.
12. Never expose Supabase service-role credentials in frontend code.
13. Protect against direct API requests that bypass the user interface.
14. Use safe database functions and server-side validation for privileged changes.
15. Keep the existing Stays authorization model intact.

If the existing `is_platform_admin()` function or equivalent is already present and correctly implemented, reuse it rather than creating a duplicate.

Build employee permission helpers that are secure, centralized and reusable.

Do not trust a role name or permission sent from the frontend without verifying it against authenticated server-side records.

Never use local storage as the authority for a user's role or permissions.

